# List04 单词


## expense
- **音标**: /ɪkˈspens/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 费用；开支
- **例句**: Travel expenses will be covered by the company.
- **近义词**: cost, charge
- **派生词**: expenditure (n.)

## exploit
- **音标**: /ɪkˈsplɔɪt/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 开发；利用；剥削
- **例句**: We must exploit every opportunity to learn.
- **近义词**: utilize, take advantage of
- **派生词**: exploitation (n.)

## explore
- **音标**: /ɪkˈsplɔːr/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 探索；考察
- **例句**: Scientists explore the depths of the ocean.
- **近义词**: investigate, examine
- **派生词**: exploration (n.)

## expose
- **音标**: /ɪkˈspoʊz/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 暴露；揭露
- **例句**: The scandal was exposed by the media.
- **近义词**: reveal, uncover
- **派生词**: exposure (n.)

## extend
- **音标**: /ɪkˈstend/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 延伸；扩展
- **例句**: The deadline has been extended by one week.
- **近义词**: stretch, prolong
- **派生词**: extension (n.)

## extent
- **音标**: /ɪkˈstent/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 程度；范围
- **例句**: To what extent do you agree with this statement?
- **近义词**: degree, scope
- **派生词**: —

## external
- **音标**: /ɪkˈstɜːrnl/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 外部的；外面的
- **例句**: External factors may affect the outcome.
- **近义词**: outer, outside
- **派生词**: externally (adv.)

## extraordinary
- **音标**: /ɪkˈstrɔːrdneri/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 非凡的；特别的
- **例句**: She has extraordinary talent in music.
- **近义词**: remarkable, exceptional
- **派生词**: extraordinarily (adv.)

## extreme
- **音标**: /ɪkˈstriːm/
- **词性**: adj. n.
- **释义**: 极端的；极度的
- **例句**: Extreme weather events are becoming more frequent.
- **近义词**: severe, intense
- **派生词**: extremely (adv.)

## facilitate
- **音标**: /fəˈsɪlɪteɪt/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 促进；使便利
- **例句**: Technology facilitates communication.
- **近义词**: ease, promote
- **派生词**: facility (n.)

## factor
- **音标**: /ˈfæktər/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 因素；因子
- **例句**: Cost is an important factor in the decision.
- **近义词**: element, component
- **派生词**: —

## fade
- **音标**: /feɪd/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 褪色；消退
- **例句**: The memory gradually faded away.
- **近义词**: dim, vanish
- **派生词**: —

## failure
- **音标**: /ˈfeɪljər/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 失败；故障
- **例句**: Failure is the mother of success.
- **近义词**: defeat, breakdown
- **派生词**: fail (v.)

## fashion
- **音标**: /ˈfæʃn/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 时尚；方式
- **例句**: She is always dressed in the latest fashion.
- **近义词**: style, trend
- **派生词**: fashionable (adj.)

## fatal
- **音标**: /ˈfeɪtl/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 致命的；毁灭性的
- **例句**: The accident was fatal to three passengers.
- **近义词**: deadly, lethal
- **派生词**: fatally (adv.)

## feature
- **音标**: /ˈfiːtʃər/
- **词性**: n. v.
- **释义**: 特征；特色；以……为特色
- **例句**: The phone has many new features.
- **近义词**: characteristic, trait
- **派生词**: —

## fierce
- **音标**: /fɪrs/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 激烈的；凶猛的
- **例句**: Competition in the market is fierce.
- **近义词**: intense, violent
- **派生词**: fiercely (adv.)

## figure
- **音标**: /ˈfɪɡjər/
- **词性**: n. v.
- **释义**: 数字；人物；认为
- **例句**: The figure shows a significant increase.
- **近义词**: number, shape
- **派生词**: —

## flexible
- **音标**: /ˈfleksəbl/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 灵活的；可变通的
- **例句**: We need a more flexible approach.
- **近义词**: adaptable, versatile
- **派生词**: flexibility (n.)

## flock
- **音标**: /flɒk/
- **词性**: v. n.
- **释义**: 群集；成群
- **例句**: Tourists flock to the beach every summer.
- **近义词**: gather, swarm
- **派生词**: —

